{"name":"Melted Wax","hex":"#f6e6c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"melted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of melt"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being in a liquid state as a result of melting.","Cooked thoroughly enough to break down resulting in a rich, jammy, buttery or similar mouthfeel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melted"},{"term":"wax","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Watam."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any oily, water-resistant, solid or semisolid substance; normally long-chain hydrocarbons, alcohols or esters.","Beeswax (a wax secreted by bees)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wax"}],"entries":[{"title":"Melted","blocks":[{"text":"Melted is the third album by American garage rock singer-songwriter Ty Segall. It was released on June 15, 2010 on Goner Records, on CD/LP formats. The songs \"My Sunshine\" and \"Caesar\" were officially released as singles, and \"Girlfriend\" had an official music video."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/Ty_Segall_-_Melted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melted","wikidata":"Q15912022"},{"title":"Wax","blocks":[{"text":"Waxes are a diverse class of organic compounds that are lipophilic solids that are malleable near ambient temperatures. They include higher alkanes and lipids, typically with melting points above about 40 °C (104 °F), melting to give low viscosity liquids. Waxes are insoluble in water but soluble in nonpolar organic solvents such as hexane, benzene and chloroform. Natural waxes of various types are produced by plants and animals and occur in petroleum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Beeswax_foundation.jpg/330px-Beeswax_foundation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"